      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive; takes the を object.\n\nWritten with {聴|き}く rather than {聞|き}く when the listening is attentive and deliberate — music, a concert, a lecture. Both are read きく.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {聞|き}く: to hear; to ask — the everyday, broader word for perceiving sound or asking a question\n- {聴|き}く: to listen attentively — emphasizes focused, appreciative listening",
